](else:)[
# LNG-D3: Identify a function

Room: Teacher Lounge

Difficulty: Easy

Value: 4 points

Write this code on your paper before solving: **LNG-D3**

Is this relation a function? (0,1), (1,2), (2,3), (3,4)

(link: "A. Yes, each input has one output")[(goto: "LNG Day 3 Correct")]

(link: "B. No, an input repeats")[(goto: "LNG Day 3 Wrong")]

(link: "C. No, the outputs repeat")[(goto: "LNG Day 3 Wrong")]

(link: "D. Yes, because all outputs are positive")[(goto: "LNG Day 3 Wrong")]
]

:: LNG Day 3 Correct
(if: $lngd3Done)[
# LNG-D3: Already Locked

This puzzle was already attempted. No extra points can be earned.

(link: "Return to Teacher Lounge")[(goto: "LNG Room")]
](else:)[
(set: $lngd3Done to true)(set: $score to $score + 4)(set: $puzzlesAttempted to $puzzlesAttempted + 1)(set: $puzzlesCorrect to $puzzlesCorrect + 1)
# Correct: LNG-D3

You win the Copper Copy Card.

+4 points

Correct answer: Yes, each input has one output

Explanation: A relation is a function if each input has only one output. Here 0, 1, 2, and 3 each appear once.

Current score: $score points

(link: "Return to Teacher Lounge")[(goto: "LNG Room")]

(link: "Return to Main Hall")[(goto: "Main Hall")]
